#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Run-2-nodes-in-single-or-separate-docker-containers.rst:9
msgid "Running ROS 2 nodes in Docker [community-contributed]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Run-2-nodes-in-single-or-separate-docker-containers.rst:12
msgid "Run two nodes in a single docker container"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Run-2-nodes-in-single-or-separate-docker-containers.rst:14
msgid "Pull the ROS docker image with tag \"rolling-desktop\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Run-2-nodes-in-single-or-separate-docker-containers.rst:16
msgid "$ docker pull osrf/ros:rolling-desktop"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Run-2-nodes-in-single-or-separate-docker-containers.rst:21
msgid "Run the image in a container in interactive mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Run-2-nodes-in-single-or-separate-docker-containers.rst:23
msgid "$ docker run -it osrf/ros:rolling-desktop"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Run-2-nodes-in-single-or-separate-docker-containers.rst:27
msgid "Your best friend is the ``ros2`` command line help now."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Run-2-nodes-in-single-or-separate-docker-containers.rst:29
msgid "$ ros2 --help"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Run-2-nodes-in-single-or-separate-docker-containers.rst:33
msgid "E.g. list all installed packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Run-2-nodes-in-single-or-separate-docker-containers.rst:35
msgid ""
"$ ros2 pkg list\n"
"(you will see a list of packages)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Run-2-nodes-in-single-or-separate-docker-containers.rst:41
msgid "E.g. list all executables:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Run-2-nodes-in-single-or-separate-docker-containers.rst:43
msgid ""
"$ ros2 pkg executables\n"
"(you will see a list of <package> <executable>)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Run-2-nodes-in-single-or-separate-docker-containers.rst:49
msgid ""
"Run a minimal example of 2 C++ nodes (1 topic subscriber ``listener``, 1 "
"topic publisher ``talker``) from the package ``demo_nodes_cpp`` in this "
"container:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Run-2-nodes-in-single-or-separate-docker-containers.rst:51
msgid ""
"$ ros2 run demo_nodes_cpp listener &\n"
"$ ros2 run demo_nodes_cpp talker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Run-2-nodes-in-single-or-separate-docker-containers.rst:57
msgid "Run two nodes in two separate docker containers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Run-2-nodes-in-single-or-separate-docker-containers.rst:59
msgid ""
"Open a terminal. Run the image in a container in interactive mode and launch "
"a topic publisher (executable ``talker`` from the package "
"``demo_nodes_cpp``) with ``ros2 run``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Run-2-nodes-in-single-or-separate-docker-containers.rst:62
msgid ""
"$ docker run -it --rm osrf/ros:rolling-desktop ros2 run demo_nodes_cpp talker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Run-2-nodes-in-single-or-separate-docker-containers.rst:66
msgid ""
"Open a second terminal. Run the image in a container in interactive mode and "
"launch a topic subscriber (executable ``listener`` from the package "
"``demo_nodes_cpp``)  with ``ros2 run``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Run-2-nodes-in-single-or-separate-docker-containers.rst:69
msgid ""
"$ docker run -it --rm osrf/ros:rolling-desktop ros2 run demo_nodes_cpp "
"listener"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Run-2-nodes-in-single-or-separate-docker-containers.rst:73
msgid ""
"As an alternative to the command line invocation, you can create a ``docker-"
"compose.yml`` file (here version 2) with the following (minimal) content:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Run-2-nodes-in-single-or-separate-docker-containers.rst:75
msgid ""
"version: '2'\n"
"\n"
"services:\n"
"  talker:\n"
"    image: osrf/ros:rolling-desktop\n"
"    command: ros2 run demo_nodes_cpp talker\n"
"  listener:\n"
"    image: osrf/ros:rolling-desktop\n"
"    command: ros2 run demo_nodes_cpp listener\n"
"    depends_on:\n"
"      - talker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Run-2-nodes-in-single-or-separate-docker-containers.rst:89
msgid ""
"To run the containers call ``docker compose up`` in the same directory. You "
"can close the containers with ``Ctrl+C``."
msgstr ""
